-- title:
--   A Hecke coordinate on inertia-displaced Eisenstein 2-torsion
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and let $B$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lying over $2$ in the sense that $2$ belongs to the nonunits of $B$. Give $JZero\ p$, the group of degree-zero divisor classes of the base-changed full modular function field of level $p$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, the `HeckeAlg`-module structure `heckeModuleBar p`, where `HeckeAlg` is the polynomial ring $\mathbb{Z}[X_\ell : \ell \text{ prime}]$. The assertion is that there is a natural number $C$, independent of $m$, such that for every $m$ the subgroup $G_m$ of $JZero\ p$ obtained as the intersection of `eisensteinTorsionBar p 2 m` (the elements annihilated by the $m$-th power of the Eisenstein maximal ideal at $2$) with the subgroup generated by all displacements $\sigma \cdot x - x$ with $\sigma$ in the image in $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ of the inertia subgroup of $B$ and $x$ in `eisensteinTorsionBar p 2 M` for some $M$, admits an additive group homomorphism $\iota$ into the quotient of `heckeLatticeAlgebra p ∅` — the image of the Hecke algebra of weight-two cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(p)$ inside $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb{Z}}$ of the integral lattice — by the ideal generated by $2^m$, such that: for every $t \in$ `HeckeAlg` and every $x \in G_m$ with $t \cdot x \in G_m$ one has $\iota(t\cdot x) = \overline{\lambda(\text{heckeEvalForms } p\ 2\ t)}\,\iota(x)$, where `heckeEvalForms` sends the variable at $\ell$ to $U_\ell$ if $\ell \mid p$ and to $T_\ell$ otherwise and $\lambda$ is the induced map to the lattice algebra; and $\iota$ has kernel of cardinality at most $2^C$.
--
--   This is the rank-one statement for the Eisenstein torsion of $J_0(p)$ met with the subgroup of inertia displacements at a place above $2$, in the form used for level lowering: a single Hecke-equivariant coordinate with values in $\mathbb{T}^L/2^m$, the uniform constant $C$ absorbing the defect rather than a Gorenstein hypothesis. It is the input to [`ModularCurve.exists_addSubgroup_le_eisensteinTorsionBar_inertia_smul_sub_mem_addMonoidHom_heckeLatticeAlgebra_quotient_natCard_ker_le`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_addSubgroup_le_eisensteinTorsionBar_inertia_smul_sub_mem_addMonoidHom_heckeLatticeAlgebra_quotient_natCard_ker_le).
